      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I am deeply sorry you are going through such a painful and isolating time after your injury. It is completely understandable to feel like a \"ghost\" when a major part of your life and self suddenly vanishes, and the silence you feel is often a direct result of that sudden loss.\n\nPlease remember that healing is a gradual process, and the \"quiet\" you describe is often the very first step toward a different kind of peace, not the end of who you are. I encourage you to try to be gentle with yourself and consider speaking to a therapist who can help you navigate this profound sense of loss and help you slowly feel your way back to a self you can recognize again.",
